    "result_text": "The full build is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment (`<LAST3>-<NNNN>`) with minimal structural impact by adding behavior as small, cohesive units rather than growing any existing class or method.\n\n**New self-contained unit (WMC_other = 0):**\n- `AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java` \u2014 a one-method OfficeFloor function that reads `@Val Owner`, computes `LAST3` from the upper-cased first three letters of the last name and `NNNN` as `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1`, and sets the code. Runs before `SaveOwner`, so the new owner isn't yet counted (matches the \"one more than current owners\" rule and the test's `cb == ca + 1` invariant).\n\n**Minimal edits to existing files:**\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added the `customerCode` field plus a trivial getter/setter (unavoidable, since the value must persist and be read back via a separate `GET`).\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `assignCustomerCode` step between `rejectDuplicateTelephone` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added `customerCode` as a read-only property on the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it (MapStruct maps it by name automatically \u2014 no mapper change needed).\n- `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `customer_code` column.\n- `db/hsqldb/data.sql` \u2014 extended the seed `owners` inserts with a trailing `NULL` to match the new column count.\n\nNo existing function bodies were modified beyond the two trivial accessors, and the derivation logic lives in a fresh class with no surrounding complexity.",
